.TH MU2EDAQ\-DOWNTIME\-LOGGER\-API 7 "2026-10-06" "mu2edaq-downtime-logger 0.1.0" "Mu2e DAQ Manual"
.SH NAME
mu2edaq\-downtime\-logger\-api \- downtime logger HTTP API and wire protocols
.SH DESCRIPTION
This page describes what
.BR mu2edaq\-downtime\-logger (1)
exposes over HTTP and what each shipped detector expects to receive.
.SH HTTP API
Served by a stdlib
.B ThreadingHTTPServer
on a daemon thread when
.B webserver.enabled
is true; address and port from
.BR mu2edaq\-downtime\-logger.yaml (5).
Only
.B GET
is implemented; other methods get the
.B http.server
default 501.
There is no authentication and no TLS.
Every response carries
.BR "Cache\-Control: no\-store" .
Unknown paths return 404
.IR "not found" ;
an exception in a handler returns 500 with
.BI "internal error: " text
in the body.
.TP
.BR "GET /" ", " "GET /index.html"
HTML status page with a meta refresh of
.BR refresh_seconds .
Banner, detector table, active event, last
.B history_limit
events.
.TP
.B GET /report
HTML summary over a time window.
Query parameters
.B from
and
.B to
in
.B YYYY\-MM\-DDTHH:MM
or
.BR YYYY\-MM\-DDTHH:MM:SS ,
interpreted as UTC.
Default: the last 7 days.
A reversed range is swapped.
An unparseable value returns 500.
.TP
.B GET /api/status
JSON object:
.RS
.TP
.B score
float, the last metric score.
.TP
.B is_down
the metric's verdict at the last recompute.
It is reported even while monitoring is disabled, when no event can open;
the enabled state itself is not exposed.
.TP
.B updated_at
ISO\-8601 with offset.
.TP
.B readings
array of
.RB { detector_id ,
.BR state " (" up | down | unknown ),
.BR weight ,
.BR ts ,
.BR detail }.
.TP
.B current_event
the event the state machine holds open, or null.
.RE
.TP
.B GET /api/events
JSON array of the newest
.B history_limit
events by
.BR started_at .
Each event:
.BR id ,
.BR started_at ,
.BR ended_at ,
.BR duration_seconds ,
.BR opened_by ,
.BR score_at_open ,
.BR category ,
.BR subsystem ,
.BR cause ,
.BR notes ,
.BR is_open .
.TP
.BI "GET /api/events/" ID
One event, or 404.
.TP
.B GET /api/report
JSON form of
.BR /report :
.B range
.RB { from ,
.BR to },
.B summary
.RB { total_events ,
.BR total_seconds ,
.BR avg_seconds ,
.BR longest_seconds },
.BR by_category [],
.BR by_subsystem [],
.BR events [].
Durations are clamped to the window; an open event runs to
.BR to .
.B avg_seconds
averages closed events only.
.TP
.B GET /healthz
.B ok
as text/plain.
It reports that the HTTP thread is alive and nothing else.
.SS Timestamps
Events read from SQLite carry no offset: their timestamps are UTC
wall\-clock times serialized without a suffix (for example
.BR 2026\-10\-06T14:00:00 ).
Timestamps built in memory
.RB ( updated_at ,
readings,
.BR current_event )
carry
.BR +00:00 .
Treat both forms as UTC.
.SS Escaping
Detector
.B detail
strings and event text are inserted into the HTML pages without HTML
escaping.
.SH DETECTOR WIRE PROTOCOLS
.SS ZmqDetector
Opens a
.B ZMQ_SUB
socket,
.B connects
it to
.BR endpoint ,
subscribes to
.BR topic .
The peer must be a
.B ZMQ_PUB
that binds.
Each frame is decoded as UTF\-8 (errors replaced), stripped, lowercased,
and tested with Python substring containment:
.IP \(bu 2
DOWN if it contains any of
.BR stopped ,
.BR stop ,
.BR down ,
.BR halted ,
.BR abort ,
.BR aborted ;
.IP \(bu 2
else UP if it contains any of
.BR running ,
.BR run ,
.BR up ,
.BR started ,
.BR active ;
.IP \(bu 2
else UP as a heartbeat.
.PP
Matching is not word\-bounded:
.I shutdown
and
.I countdown
read DOWN,
.I setup
and
.I truncated
read UP.
Any frame restarts a watchdog of
.BR heartbeat_timeout_s ;
expiry reports DOWN with detail
.IR "no zmq messages within timeout" .
.PP
Not compatible with the
.B mu2edaq\-dashboard
message bus: the dashboard
.B binds ZMQ_PULL
on 5555 and its producers
.BR "PUSH \-connect" .
A SUB socket connected there is rejected during the ZMTP handshake and
receives nothing; the detector reports DOWN after the timeout.
Even if frames arrived, the bus JSON
.RB ( event_category ,
.BR error_level ,
.BR subsystem ,
.BR timestamp ,
.BR message )
carries no run state; it would be read as UP heartbeats, or as DOWN
whenever a message text contained a DOWN token.
.SS UdpDetector
Binds a
.B QUdpSocket
to
.IR bind : port
with address sharing.
Same grammar and watchdog as ZmqDetector, applied per datagram; expiry
detail
.IR "no udp datagrams within timeout" .
Any sender is accepted, without authentication.
.SS SoapDetector
.B zeep
client on
.BR wsdl ;
calls
.I operation
with
.I args
every
.BR poll_s ,
follows the dotted
.B state_path
through the response, lowercases the result and compares it exactly with
.B down_values
and
.BR up_values .
No match, a WSDL failure or a call failure gives UNKNOWN, never DOWN.
.SS DiskActivityDetector
No wire protocol.
A
.B watchdog
observer records the time of any non\-directory event under
.BR paths ;
a poll reports DOWN when that time is older than
.BR idle_seconds .
The initial time is the newest mtime found under
.BR paths ,
or the epoch if none.
.SS LogfileDetector
No wire protocol.
Tails each file every
.BR poll_s ,
reopening on inode change or truncation, and applies
.B down_patterns
then
.B up_patterns
with
.B re.search
to every new line.
A file that is opened for the first time, including one recreated after a
rotation gap, is read from its end.
.SH SERVICE DISCOVERY
With the web server enabled and
.B mu2edaq_discovery
importable, a
.B Responder
announces
.BR name="Downtime Logger" ,
.BR app="downtime\-logger" ,
.BR scheme=http ,
.B port=webserver.port
and the host's FQDN.
No
.B meta
is sent.
The announced address does not reflect
.BR webserver.bind :
with
.B bind: 127.0.0.1
the advertised URL is unreachable from other hosts.
